    prov:endedAtTime "2026-11-14T16:09:32Z"^^xsd:dateTime .

session:pr795Summary a agp:TranscriptSummary ;
    agp:summaryText "Issue #674 reported that BOUND/REGEX/ISBLANK/ISLITERAL/LANGMATCHES etc. silently evaluated to None when nested inside IF(...)'s condition/branches or COALESCE(...)'s arguments, breaking the W3C SHACL spec's own sh:PatternConstraintComponent example (IF(bound($flags), regex(...), regex(...))). Root cause (already diagnosed in the issue, verified by reading the code before changing anything): sparql_parser's FILTER/&&/||/! path recurses through eval_expression_bool -> eval_function_bool, which has dedicated arms for these FILTER-only builtins, but IF() and COALESCE() evaluate their arguments through a separate value-producing path (eval_expression_value_inner -> eval_function_value) that had no entries for them at all, falling through to None and short-circuiting via '?'. Wrote failing tests first: a bare IF-condition case (bound() as the IF condition), an IF-branch case (regex() in the else branch), a COALESCE case (bound() as a COALESCE argument), and the SHACL-spec pattern itself with unbound $flags (regex() in the else branch again, nested under bound() as the IF condition). All four were run and confirmed genuinely red (None instead of the expected value) before any implementation change. Then implemented the fix. A fifth test -- the SHACL-spec pattern with $flags bound, exercising the IF's *then*-branch (3-arg regex) rather than the else-branch the first four already covered -- was added afterwards to close that coverage gap; it was never observed red against the pre-fix code, though it goes through the identical code path as the already-verified else-branch case." ;
    agp:reasoningFor ghpull:795 ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy session:pr795 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo session:claudeSonnet5 .

session:pr795Summary agp:decisionPoint session:pr795Decision .

session:pr795Decision a agp:Decision ;
    agp:summaryText "Took approach (a) from the issue: gave eval_function_value its own arms for BOUND/REGEX/LANGMATCHES/ISBLANK/ISLITERAL/ISIRI/ISURI/IS_LEXICALLY_VALID that delegate to eval_function_bool and wrap the bool result as an xsd:boolean GraphElement, mirroring the existing STRSTARTS/STRENDS/CONTAINS pattern already in that function. This is recursion-safe because every one of those names is matched by eval_function_bool's own dedicated arm, never its '_ => eval_function_value(...)' fallback arm -- so eval_function_value -> eval_function_bool never calls back into eval_function_value for the same name. It also fixes COALESCE for free since both IF and COALESCE share the same value-dispatch path. ISIRI/ISURI/IS_LEXICALLY_VALID were added beyond the issue's literal list because they live in the same eval_function_bool dedicated-arm block and have the identical bug." ;
    agp:alternative "Approach (b) from the issue -- routing IF()'s condition through eval_expression_bool instead of eval_expression_value_inner when the branches are boolean-valued -- was rejected as the issue author anticipated: it requires knowing ahead of time whether a given IF() usage is in value or boolean position, which isn't generally decidable from the condition expression alone, and it would not fix COALESCE(...) at all since COALESCE has no notion of a distinguished 'condition' argument." .
